# Docker build context exclusions -- see Dockerfile's own comment on why the context
# is the repo root (Cargo workspace resolution needs every member's Cargo.toml
# present). Everything under crates/ is kept; this only trims non-source cruft that
# would otherwise bloat the context upload with no effect on the build.

target/
.git/
.github/

# Local dev tooling, not needed inside the build context
.mise.toml
mise.toml
.direnv/

# Docs and non-build metadata
docs/
*.md
LICENSE*

# Editor/OS noise
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store

# Claude Code / agent scratch state, never relevant to a container build
.claude/
